# Everything here runs on Linux (the Jetson) even when it is edited on Windows.
# A CRLF line ending in a shell script makes the kernel read the shebang as
# "/usr/bin/env bash\r" and fail with "bad interpreter", which is a confusing
# error a long way from its cause. Force LF for anything executable or parsed.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.patch text eol=lf
*.tsv   text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf

*.wav binary
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
